WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.775
Does it work in a government cloud?

2
00:00:01.775 --> 00:00:05.788
Microsoft Learn's three Zero
Trust Assessment pages don't say.

3
00:00:05.788 --> 00:00:11.219
The tool's three point one point oh
source does: its connect command takes an

4
00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:16.475
environment, Global, U S Gov or U S Gov
D O D, and an Exchange environment name.

5
00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:20.163
Each service it signs in to is
documented per cloud on Learn,

6
00:00:20.163 --> 00:00:23.775
and the guide matches the tool's
parameters to those pages.

7
00:00:23.775 --> 00:00:28.459
One place they conflict: for Security
and Compliance in D O D, Learn gives

8
00:00:28.459 --> 00:00:31.158
compliance dot D O D
dot microsoft dot com,

9
00:00:31.158 --> 00:00:34.175
and the tool's source
uses a different address.

10
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:35.963
Which one works wasn't tested.

11
00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:40.998
For SharePoint, the tool infers a
sharepoint dot U S admin address,

12
00:00:40.998 --> 00:00:44.262
so pass it explicitly;
D O D's isn't specified.

13
00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:48.431
Until a run is proved in your cloud,
run one pillar at a time in a test

14
00:00:48.431 --> 00:00:53.110
tenant of the same cloud, and keep
ScubaGear as the federal baseline tool.
